    "title": "Crowds gather for Chicopee's National Night Out celebration - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CHICOPEE, Mass. (WWLP) – National Night Out events continue across the region, connecting first responders with the community. Wednesday night, hundreds gathered for the city of Chicopee’s 31st year of the celebration at Sarah Jane Sherman Park. The free community event featured a variety of engaging activities. But most importantly, residents got to meet with local law enforcement and other emergency personnel in a more inviting environment. Chicopee Officer Travis Odiorne, Spokesperson for Chicopee PD, told 22News, “There’s a human side to policing. At the end of the day, we go home—we take off our uniforms. We are all moms, dads, husbands, and wives. We want them to know that we are here too as part of the community.” WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Watch the 22News Digital Edition weekdays at 4 p.m. on WWLP.com. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WWLP.",
